    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe driver initially ticks no blackouts and explains that he sometimes misses radio messages because of reduced hearing, but later describes a delivery during which his colleague waved in front of him for several seconds before he responded; he remembers hearing the engine and seeing the loading bay, although he cannot recall the spoken exchange. The colleague believes he was briefly unaware, while the driver thinks his hearing aid battery had failed, and neither account establishes whether consciousness was lost.\n\nHe has a history of noise exposure and uses one hearing aid inconsistently; a screening sheet lists left-ear thresholds of 45 dB at 500 Hz and 50 dB at 1000 Hz, but provides no right-ear values or results at 2000 and 3000 Hz. He reports no hearing loss in quiet conversation, yet repeatedly asks the nurse to repeat questions when a fan is running, and there is no signed audiologist assessment.\n\nA similar pause may have happened three weeks earlier after poor sleep, although he cannot confirm the date and there is no witness report. Neurological review has been requested and no cause is established; the nurse has recorded the hearing difficulty and the disputed awareness episodes separately rather than assuming that one explains the other.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
